FFmpeg — notice
===============

AVAR Kantar uses FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org) through Qt Multimedia to play
IP-camera streams. Avar Elektronik has NOT modified FFmpeg.

  Version     7.1.5  (measured from the shipped DLLs: av_version_info)
  Files       avcodec-61.dll, avformat-61.dll, avutil-59.dll,
              swresample-5.dll, swscale-8.dll
              Separate, dynamically loaded libraries in the program folder.
              You may replace them with your own compatible build of the
              same major versions.
  Built by    The Qt Company, as part of the Qt for Python binaries
              (PySide6-Addons 6.11.2).
  License     GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later
              -> LGPL-2.1.txt (upstream statement: ffmpeg-LICENSE.md)
              The build configuration below contains none of
              --enable-gpl, --enable-version3 or --enable-nonfree, so no
              GPL or LGPLv3 parts are included and the LGPL v2.1+ applies.
  Copyright   Copyright (c) the FFmpeg developers.

Configuration of the shipped build (avcodec_configuration):
  --prefix=/c/FFmpeg-n7.1.5/build/msvc/installed --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-debug --enable-network --disable-lzma --enable-pic --disable-vulkan --disable-v4l2-m2m --disable-decoder=truemotion1 --disable-avdevice --disable-avfilter --enable-zlib --extra-cflags='-IC:/zlib-1.3.1/build/amd64' --extra-ldflags='-LIBPATH:C:/zlib-1.3.1/build/amd64' --toolchain=msvc --enable-shared --disable-static

Corresponding source code:
  https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.5.tar.xz
  Qt's attribution page for this component:
  https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtmultimedia-attribution-ffmpeg.html
  The build scripts for Qt's prebuilt FFmpeg binaries are in the Qt
  git repository (https://code.qt.io).
